cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "pic-geo: Polymer Industry Cluster county footprints and ZIP-to-county crosswalk"
message: >-
  If you use these definitions or this crosswalk, please cite this repository and the version
  you used. County footprints are organizational decisions that can change, and the crosswalk
  is built on the 2020 decennial ZCTA vintage, so a figure quoted without a version is not
  reproducible. Cite the U.S. Census Bureau 2020 ZCTA-to-county relationship file as the
  upstream source of the ZIP assignments.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Polymer Industry Cluster, Greater Akron Chamber"
    city: Akron
    region: Ohio
    country: US
    website: "https://picinnovation.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/polymerindustrycluster/pic-geo"
abstract: >-
  The two Northeast Ohio county footprints the Polymer Industry Cluster measures against —
  PIC-12, used for federal-data analyses, and NEO-14, used for company-vault analyses — as
  code, with their FIPS codes, the ten counties they share, and the six that belong to only
  one of them. Ships an authoritative ZIP-to-county crosswalk for the PIC-12 footprint, 261
  ZCTAs and 614 observed city names, derived from the U.S. Census Bureau 2020
  ZCTA-to-county relationship file. It replaces a city list derived from facility-filed
  county names, which put out-of-region Ohio towns inside the footprint and contaminated
  published patent and award counts. Known limits, including the 18 ZCTAs with genuine
  in-footprint land that the largest-land-piece rule assigns elsewhere, are documented in
  the module docstrings and README; changes to published values are logged in CORRECTIONS.md.
keywords:
  - county footprint
  - FIPS codes
  - ZCTA
  - ZIP code crosswalk
  - Northeast Ohio
  - regional economics
  - polymers
  - reproducible research
